\ serial.ga - send 18-bit words on node 708's pin 1, to be read as
\ ga-tools' host side reads them: for each word a byte of 0, then its low,
\ middle and high bits in three bytes, and a byte of 1 at the end.
\ Bytes are a start bit, 8 data bits from the lowest, and a stop bit, on
\ the evaluation board's inverted line: pin 1 high (3) for 0, low (2) for 1.
\ B must address io.
\
\ ga-tools' unext_baud is a bit time at its --baud over 2.4 ns, and
\ `unext_baud for unext` runs one more unext than that, leaving nothing for
\ the code around the loop. At 921600 baud, waits from 6 to 54 unexts
\ shorter decode, so this waits 30 shorter, about 72 ns, to sit in the
\ middle; at slower bauds the code is a smaller part of a bit.

: wait unext_baud -30 + for unext ;
: level ( n ) !b wait ;
: bits ( c ) 3 level 7 for dup - 1 and 2 + level 2/ next drop 2 level ;
: send ( w )
    0 bits dup bits
    2/ 2/ 2/ 2/ 2/ 2/ 2/ 2/ dup bits
    2/ 2/ 2/ 2/ 2/ 2/ 2/ 2/ bits ;
: done 1 bits ;
